=1 5 3
+    sdcard.c
=1 9 3
+    This module implements the hard disk boot driver for the Raspberry Pi
+    (the ARM BOOT\LIB\SCSIDISK.C ScsiDiskEntryTable) over its SD card, the
+    system disk, which sits on the EMMC controller of the BCM2836 and BCM2837
+    (an Arasan SD host controller, SDHCI 3.0) or on the EMMC2 controller of the
+    BCM2711 (SDHCI 3.0), the only one wired to the card slot of a Raspberry
+    Pi 4. The card is disk 0 of SCSI adapter 0, the adapter the configuration
+    tree describes: scsi(0)disk(0)rdisk(0).
+
+    The controller is driven by programmed I/O: each 512-byte block passes
+    through the data port. Card bring-up follows the SD physical layer
+    specification: CMD0, CMD8, ACMD41, CMD2, CMD3, CMD9 (capacity), CMD7,
+    ACMD6 (4-bit bus). A standard capacity card is byte addressed, a high
+    capacity card block addressed.
+
+    The EMMC loses a register write that follows another within two SD clocks
+    (a clock domain crossing), so every register write but the data port's is
+    followed by a delay longer than two clocks at the 400 kHz identification
+    clock.
+
+    The card slot is on GPIO 48-53, which function ALT3 connects to the EMMC.
+    The VideoCore firmware of a BCM2837 board (Pi 2 v1.2, Pi 3) leaves them on
+    ALT0, its SD host controller, and connects the EMMC to the wireless chip on
+    GPIO 34-39 (ALT3 too); those pins are made inputs, so the EMMC drives the
+    slot alone. The EMMC2 has pins of its own.
=1 23 3
